17 council meeting"},{"t":", Surrey council approved"},{"t":"third reading"},{"t":"for the rezoning and land-use amendments required to advance the project."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"The development site sits near several established residential pockets"},{"t":"—including the"},{"t":"16216 20 Avenue","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/our-listings.html/listing.16216-20-avenue-surrey-c8070236.106159372"},{"t":"area—making this a significant change for long-time"},{"t":"homeowners and new buyers alike","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/selling.html"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"The proposed store at"},{"t":"1891 and 1947 164 Street"},{"t":"drew a wide range of opinions during Monday’s public hearing. Many residents voiced support, pointing out that major retailers like"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Walmart"},{"t":"and"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Real Canadian Superstore"},{"t":"already operate nearby. Some argued that blocking Costco’s arrival would create an unfair commercial environment. One attendee remarked,"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"“There’s always winners and losers in stuff like this, but I’m pro-Costco… This will also provide jobs for young people.”"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"For local neighbourhoods—such as the community around"},{"t":"16216 20 Avenue","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/our-listings.html/listing.16216-20-avenue-surrey-c8070236.106159372"},{"t":"—"},{"t":"the project represents both"},{"t":"new opportunities","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/our-listings.html"},{"t":"and new traffic considerations."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"With the updated zoning now supported by council, the project includes a"},{"t":"large-format Costco store","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/our-listings.html/listing.16216-20-avenue-surrey-c8070236.106159372"},{"t":", a"},{"t":"gas station"},{"t":", and a"},{"t":"parking area with 989 stalls"},{"t":". Portions of the site will be reclassified from"},{"t":"business/industrial"},{"t":"to"},{"t":"commercial"},{"t":", and from"},{"t":"multiple residential"},{"t":"to"},{"t":"mixed employment"},{"t":"designation—key steps outlined in the"},{"t":"Official Community Plan"},{"t":". Meanwhile, an"},{"t":"online petition"},{"t":", which had gathered more than"},{"t":"900 signatures"},{"t":", raised concerns about"},{"t":"traffic"},{"t":","},{"t":"infrastructure limits"},{"t":", and"},{"t":"public safety"},{"t":"."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Environmental considerations were also central to public commentary."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Deb Jack"},{"t":"of"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Surrey Environmental Partners"},{"t":"stated that “a thousand trees are going to be killed — alder and cottonwood,” and emphasized that the closest"},{"t":"bus stop","h":"https://www.translink.ca/"},{"t":"is 1,600 metres away, calling it an unsustainable distance. She noted that while the proposal has positive aspects, minimal action appears to be taken to protect"},{"t":"environmentally sensitive areas"},{"t":", including stream setbacks. Despite these concerns, council’s decision to pass"},{"t":"third reading"},{"t":"means the project will continue progressing."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"In a recent statement published on the"},{"t":"City of Surrey website","h":"https://www.surrey.ca/"},{"t":", Mayor"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Brenda Locke"},{"t":"welcomed the development, noting that it’s encouraging to see major employers like Costco continue to invest in Surrey."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"“It’s exciting to see this level of confidence and interest in our community”"}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"she said."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"As South Surrey prepares for this major commercial addition, stay tuned for updates and insights"},{"t":"Jared Gibbons","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/contact.html"},{"t":"will continue tracking the development to help residents stay informed about how this project may shape the community."}]},{"t":"p","parts":[{"t":"Blogs"},{"t":"All Blog Posts","h":"https://jaredgibbons.ca/blog.html/blog.html"}